  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies on macro-level regional panel data, which may obscure localized dynamics within specific cities or provinces.",
      "what": "This study analyzes the relationship between digital synergy and regional sustainable development across China using panel Tobit, threshold, and mediating effect models. The analysis reveals an overall N-shaped relationship, though regional variations exist, showing a positive linear impact in eastern China and an N-shaped pattern in the central and western regions. The mechanism operates by accelerating resource sharing and reshaping innovation models, which in turn drives green technological innovation and industrial structure upgrading.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that the impact of digital integration is non-linear and geographically uneven, proving that digital development policies must be tailored to regional contexts rather than applied as uniform solutions."
    }
